b development, and digital marketing offer the best career scope and excellent career prospects.\u00a0<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1738328347319\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>Can I get a job after completing an IT course?<\/strong><\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Yes, many IT courses are career-oriented and provide professional certifications, so you are career-ready after completing the course. Courses like graphic designing, digital marketing, and web development are best for freshers to find immediate jobs.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1738328373289\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>What are the career options after IT courses?<\/strong><\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">After completing IT courses, you can apply for various job opportunities, such as:<br\/>-Digital Marketer<br\/>-Web Developer<br\/>-SEO Analyst<br\/>-E-Commerce Specialist<br\/>-Data Analyst<br\/>-Graphic Designer<br\/>-Software Tester<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1738328405325\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>Are online IT courses worth it for commerce students?<\/strong><\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Online IT courses from top-rated and credible institutions are highly beneficial and useful. You not only get the flexibility to learn at your convenience, but you can also build practical skills through hands-on projects, adding credibility to your portfolio and enhancing your resume.\u00a0<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1738328419529\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>Which IT course is the easiest for commerce students?<\/strong><\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Courses like graphic design, digital marketing, and social media marketing are beginner-friendly and easiest for commerce students.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1738328435701\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>What certifications can enhance my IT career after 12th commerce?<\/strong><\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Some valuable certifications include:<br\/>-Google Digital Marketing Certification<br\/>-Microsoft Excel Certification<br\/>-Adobe Photoshop\/Illustrator Certifications<br\/>-AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner<br\/>-HubSpot Inbound Marketing Certification<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1738328469192\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>Which IT courses are best for freelancing opportunities?<\/strong><\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">If you are looking for freelance opportunities, you can apply for various courses, such as digital marketing, data analysis, web development, graphic design, animation and video editing, and content management.\u00a0<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1738328482571\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>Can I pursue an IT course without knowing programming?<\/strong><\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">You can apply for most IT courses, such as digital marketing, data analysis, graphic designing, and e-commerce management, without programming knowledge. Most courses cover basics, starting every topic from scratch and gradually moving to more advanced topics.\u00a0<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1738328496824\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>Is a degree necessary to succeed in the IT field after commerce?<\/strong><\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">You don\u2019t need a college degree to be successful in the IT field. However, you must have skill-based certifications and hands-on experience that can outweigh formal education.\u00a0<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1738328515177\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>What are the salary prospects after completing IT courses?<\/strong><\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Salary prospects after completing IT courses depend on the field and sector in which you work. For example, a graphic designer can earn between \u20b92-5 LPA, while a digital marketer can earn between \u20b9-7 LPA. The average salary of a web developer in the beginning is between \u20b94-7 LPA, whereas a data analyst can make between \u20b94-8 LPA.\u00a0<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1738328534412\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>Can I pursue IT courses along with my B.Com degree?<\/strong><\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Yes, you can pursue a part-time IT course with your B.Com degree. Prefer online courses as they provide you with the flexibility to learn anytime.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1738328559694\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>How can I start my IT career after completing 12th commerce?<\/strong><\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Once you complete your 12th commerce, start exploring various courses and degrees you can pursue based on your interest. Apply for a suitable course and get certifications from a reputed institute. Gain hands-on experience, build a strong portfolio, and apply for freelance, internship, or beginner-level job opportunities.<\/p> <\/div> <\/div>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/digital-marketing-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=Content_Banner&amp;utm_campaign=SEO&amp;utm_page=\/it-courses-after-12th-commerce\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\" noreferrer noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1546\" height=\"380\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/best-digital-marketing-course.webp\" alt=\"Best Digital Marketing Course\" class=\"wp-image-14518\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/best-digital-marketing-course.webp 